BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w8-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260823
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260824
SUMMARY:○ OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min - Sunday is now a REST day by de
 fault. Take the ride only if you feel good and Monday's run is easy. Wit
 h a quality session on Monday you need this rest more than you need the 
 ride.\n\nWeek 8 of 17 - Build\nPoles introduced this week. They save lit
 tle metabolically but cut RPE 14-18% and measurably reduce muscle damage
  over a climb-and-descent day. Length = height x 0.67 = 107 cm\, so 105 
 cm is the correct fit (Mountain King chart: 155-165 cm -> 105 cm). Nobod
 y manufactures 93 cm - 100 cm is the shortest size made. Decathlon only 
 sells 110/120/130\, and its own chart puts 155-171 cm on 110\, which is 
 also what sub-165 cm coaches actually run. Buy the Kiprun 500 aluminium 
 at 110 cm\, EUR 70. Aluminium bends where carbon snaps\, which is the ri
 ght failure mode on wet basalt for a first-time pole user. Ultra X's 202
 6 race rules contain no restriction on poles.\n70 days to Ultra X Madeir
 a 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
