SUMMARY:NEW SPEED SLOT (5 km)
DESCRIPTION:NEW SPEED SLOT - easy 5 km with the LAST 1 KM at threshold ef
 fort. Comfortably hard\, three or four words at a time\, HR 172-181 (LTH
 R measured 181 on the 7 Sep time trial\, where 182 was held for 26 min -
  the old 168-176 band was set before there was a real number). One kilom
 etre\, that is all. This is a progression run\, not an interval session:
  you get a real quality stimulus for almost no recovery cost\, in a week
  where vertical also goes 45 to 55 min and the long day goes 1:50 to 2:0
 5. Volume is the thing being added this week - the last km is a taste\, 
 not the point.\n\nWeek 8 of 17 - Build\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the clim
 bs. Talk test.\nPoles introduced this week. They save little metabolical
 ly but cut RPE 14-18% and measurably reduce muscle damage over a climb-a
 nd-descent day. Length = height x 0.67 = 107 cm\, so 105 cm is the corre
 ct fit (Mountain King chart: 155-165 cm -> 105 cm). Nobody manufactures 
 93 cm - 100 cm is the shortest size made. Decathlon only sells 110/120/1
 30\, and its own chart puts 155-171 cm on 110\, which is also what sub-1
 65 cm coaches actually run. Buy the Kiprun 500 aluminium at 110 cm\, EUR
  70. Aluminium bends where carbon snaps\, which is the right failure mod
 e on wet basalt for a first-time pole user. Ultra X's 2026 race rules co
 ntain no restriction on poles.\n69 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
