DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260902
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260903
SUMMARY:◆ Legs ONLY\, no upper
DESCRIPTION:Legs ONLY\, no upper - heavy eccentric. Three quad lifts doin
 g three different jobs: HEAVY BILATERAL trap-bar deadlift 4 x 4-6 at 85 
 kg (18 Aug: 75x6x3 with 4+ reps in reserve\, so 1RM is nearer 100 - auto
 regulate to 2 REPS IN RESERVE and add 5 kg when the last set still feels
  easy)\, LOADED UNILATERAL Bulgarian split squat 3 x 8/leg with dumbbell
 s\, and TEMPO ECCENTRIC step-downs 3 x 8-10/leg with 3-4 s lowering. The
 n Nordics 3 x 5 and single-leg calf raises. Never to failure. 48-72 h be
 fore the long day. On a -15% descent hip drop is 23.7 mm vs 7.6 mm uphil
 l (very large effect)\, so descending is a frontal-plane hip problem and
  not only a quad problem - loaded Bulgarians carry that demand\, which i
 s why standalone side planks and cable abduction came out. HYROX SLED TE
 CHNIQUE at the end\, 8-10 x 12.5 m at 50-65% load (~100 kg)\, 60-90 s re
 st. TECHNIQUE ONLY\, never to fatigue. Forearms hooked on the posts\, 30
 -45 deg lean\, short choppy steps 20-30 cm at 3-4 per second\, and never
  let the sled stop. Sled push is PURELY CONCENTRIC\, so it costs your de
 scent block nothing - which is why it is the one Hyrox station you can t
 rain now. At 56 kg you need 1.03x bodyweight of horizontal force to brea
 k a stationary sled versus 0.81x to keep one rolling\, so learning not t
 o stop is worth more to you than to anyone heavier. About 8 minutes.\n\n
 Week 9 of 17 - Build\nGUT TRAINING STARTS. Target 60-80 g carb/h by week
  14\, from 40-50 now\, +10 g every two weeks. No drop bags and no crew a
 t Madeira - only ~2 checkpoints\, ~10 km apart - so you carry 400-500 g 
 of carbohydrate yourself. Rehearse the weight and the stowage\, not just
  the products. INTENSITY STARTS THIS WEEK\, on flat ground: Thursday's v
 ertical stays STEADY because Hyrox is 8 x 1 km flat and stair fitness do
 es not transfer. Target distribution is 80-85% easy\, 15-20% hard. ORDER
  CHANGED 31 Aug - threshold Mon -> Tue\, legs Tue -> Wed\, easy run + pu
 sh Wed -> Mon. Reason is measurement\, not fatigue: resting HR was 55 ag
 ainst a 50-52 baseline and HRV 78 against an 89 weekly average\, which d
 istorts the HR-work relationship in both directions. This is the first s
 tructured interval session of the block and its job is to establish what
  threshold feels like - a reference set on a distorted day gets trained 
 off for weeks. Load is unchanged: three runs\, two gym sessions\, one ve
 rtical\, one rest day\, Friday still free. Legs on Wednesday keeps 72 h 
 before the long day\, the outer edge of the 48-72 h rule. Push stays pai
 red with the easy run\, pull with the vertical. STOPPING RULE: the thres
 hold session happens Tuesday regardless of readiness unless sleep is und
 er 6 h or HRV drops below 70.\n60 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
