BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w10-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:○ OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min - Sunday is now a REST day by de
 fault. Take the ride only if you feel good and Monday's run is easy. Wit
 h a quality session on Monday you need this rest more than you need the 
 ride.\n\nWeek 10 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volume.
 \nCutback. Deliberate\, and the reason matters: in trail runners\, injur
 y weeks were preceded by load DROPPING 16-24% then rebounding 15-37%. Yo
 -yo loading\, not absolute load\, is what precedes injury. This dip is p
 lanned and the rebound is controlled. RESHUFFLED 6 Sep: time trial held 
 on Monday (Sunday is a full rest day\, which is the setup a TT wants - 9
 .6 h sleep and HRV 98 the night before)\, pull moved to Tuesday as the r
 ecovery day\, legs to Wednesday\, easy 5 km to Friday\, and Thursday's s
 tairwell session replaced by casual football. Three runs held: TT\, Frid
 ay easy\, Saturday long. Push moved Wednesday -> Tuesday: Tuesday is now
  a single upper day and Wednesday is legs only. Easy run moved Friday ->
  Tuesday to sit directly after the time trial: hard/easy back to back fo
 r the train-low effect\, and it moves run #3 out of the post-football Fr
 iday slot that has been the one getting skipped. Friday is now empty\, w
 hich is the better setup for Saturday. Upper moved Tuesday -> Thursday m
 orning: Tuesday is now the easy run alone\, and the upper session sits ~
 12 h before football on legs it does not touch. TIME TRIAL RESULT 7 Sep:
  5.01 km in 26:17 timer (31:20 elapsed - two auto-paused stops of 2.2 an
 d 2.9 min)\, avg HR 182\, peak 193\, cadence 179. Splits 5:05 / 5:17 / 5
 :28 / 5:14 / 5:12. Previous best 5 km was 29:15 on 15 Mar\, so a 36 s/km
  improvement. NOT a clean continuous 5 km: 81% of it sat at or above LTH
 R against 5% in the 1 Sep threshold session\, and it opened at 4:09/km f
 or 200 m. Baseline established: 5:15/km sustainable in 8-10 min blocks a
 t HR 181-183\, LTHR 181\, form holds at 178-184 spm and 100-107 cm strid
 e under duress. SUPERSEDED 8 Sep: retest set for Wednesday 16 September.
  Stream review showed the first 100 m ran at 3:50-4:00/km and 390 W with
  LTHR reached at 65 seconds\, so 7 Sep measured a pacing error rather th
 an fitness - it is not a retest but the first properly executed attempt.
  Wednesday\, not Monday\, so it sits three days clear of the Saturday lo
 ng day instead of 40 hours. The 24 November trial in Hyrox week 2 still 
 stands as the fitness comparison. NOT A REAL DOWN WEEK IN PRACTICE: volu
 me is down but intensity is not - a maximal time trial on Monday\, an ho
 ur of football on Thursday and 500 m of vertical on Saturday is three ha
 rd days. Keep Tuesday and Friday genuinely easy\, and if the shins are s
 till talking by Thursday\, football is the session that gives\, not Satu
 rday.\n56 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w10-s1-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260908
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260909
SUMMARY:Easy run 35 MIN (talk test) (4.8 km)
DESCRIPTION:Easy run 35 MIN (talk test) - THE DAY AFTER THE TIME TRIAL\, 
 deliberately. This is the one easy run in the week that does more than a
 dd volume: you start it with glycogen partially depleted from Monday\, a
 nd mitochondrial signalling is amplified when a session begins in that s
 tate. Do NOT carb-load for it - a light breakfast or fasted is the point
 . Eat normally the rest of the day and eat properly after Monday's TT\; 
 train-low applies to the session\, not the day. Keep it genuinely easy\,
  HR under 155\, it is not a workout. NO STRIDES - nothing sharp two days
  after a max effort. Tuesday is this run and nothing else. PRESCRIBED IN
  MINUTES\, not kilometres: at 7:20/km your 5 km was 36 min\, and the acc
 epted easy-run band is 30-75 min. Kilometres make the dose shrink as you
  get faster\, which is backwards.\n\nWeek 10 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - 
 recover\, do not add volume.\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk t
 est.\nCutback. Deliberate\, and the reason matters: in trail runners\, i
 njury weeks were preceded by load DROPPING 16-24% then rebounding 15-37%
 . Yo-yo loading\, not absolute load\, is what precedes injury. This dip 
 is planned and the rebound is controlled. RESHUFFLED 6 Sep: time trial h
 eld on Monday (Sunday is a full rest day\, which is the setup a TT wants
  - 9.6 h sleep and HRV 98 the night before)\, pull moved to Tuesday as t
 he recovery day\, legs to Wednesday\, easy 5 km to Friday\, and Thursday
 's stairwell session replaced by casual football. Three runs held: TT\, 
 Friday easy\, Saturday long. Push moved Wednesday -> Tuesday: Tuesday is
  now a single upper day and Wednesday is legs only. Easy run moved Frida
 y -> Tuesday to sit directly after the time trial: hard/easy back to bac
 k for the train-low effect\, and it moves run #3 out of the post-footbal
 l Friday slot that has been the one getting skipped. Friday is now empty
 \, which is the better setup for Saturday. Upper moved Tuesday -> Thursd
 ay morning: Tuesday is now the easy run alone\, and the upper session si
 ts ~12 h before football on legs it does not touch. TIME TRIAL RESULT 7 
 Sep: 5.01 km in 26:17 timer (31:20 elapsed - two auto-paused stops of 2.
 2 and 2.9 min)\, avg HR 182\, peak 193\, cadence 179. Splits 5:05 / 5:17
  / 5:28 / 5:14 / 5:12. Previous best 5 km was 29:15 on 15 Mar\, so a 36 
 s/km improvement. NOT a clean continuous 5 km: 81% of it sat at or above
