SUMMARY:◆ Legs ONLY\, no upper
DESCRIPTION:Legs ONLY\, no upper - maintenance. Volume down\, load held a
 t 80%+ 1RM. HYROX SLED TECHNIQUE at the end\, 8-10 x 12.5 m at 50-65% lo
 ad (~100 kg)\, 60-90 s rest. TECHNIQUE ONLY\, never to fatigue. Forearms
  hooked on the posts\, 30-45 deg lean\, short choppy steps 20-30 cm at 3
 -4 per second\, and never let the sled stop. Sled push is PURELY CONCENT
 RIC\, so it costs your descent block nothing - which is why it is the on
 e Hyrox station you can train now. At 56 kg you need 1.03x bodyweight of
  horizontal force to break a stationary sled versus 0.81x to keep one ro
 lling\, so learning not to stop is worth more to you than to anyone heav
 ier. About 8 minutes.\n\nWeek 10 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do
  not add volume.\nCutback. Deliberate\, and the reason matters: in trail
  runners\, injury weeks were preceded by load DROPPING 16-24% then rebou
 nding 15-37%. Yo-yo loading\, not absolute load\, is what precedes injur
 y. This dip is planned and the rebound is controlled. RESHUFFLED 6 Sep: 
