SUMMARY:▼ DESCENT LADDER (5 min)
DESCRIPTION:DESCENT LADDER - 5 min walking DOWN stairs with 5.6 kg in the
  pack\, lift back up. About 110 m of descent. THIS IS THE SESSION THE PL
 AN USED TO BE MISSING: Madeira is 2\,003 m DOWN as well as up\, and down
 hill running causes far more muscle damage and neuromuscular fatigue tha
 n level running at the same metabolic cost. One bout protects for weeks 
 (repeated-bout effect)\, which is why this is dosed weekly and progressi
 vely rather than repeated at 5 min. Stairs build tissue tolerance\; they
  do NOT reproduce running descent mechanics\, which is what the Posbank 
 long days are for.\n\nWeek 10 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do no
 t add volume.\nCutback. Deliberate\, and the reason matters: in trail ru
 nners\, injury weeks were preceded by load DROPPING 16-24% then reboundi
 ng 15-37%. Yo-yo loading\, not absolute load\, is what precedes injury. 
