BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w11-s3-legs@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260917
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260918
SUMMARY:◆ Legs
DESCRIPTION:Legs - MOVED TO THURSDAY\, after the time trial. Heavy eccent
 ric quad work 48 h before a 5 km measures your fitness through muscle da
 mage\, which was already baked into 7 Sep. Last legs session was 25 Aug 
 - this one is not optional\, and the lower-leg capacity block in it has 
 never actually been done. Legs ONLY\, no upper - heavy eccentric. Three 
 quad lifts doing three different jobs: HEAVY BILATERAL trap-bar deadlift
  4 x 4-6 at 85 kg (18 Aug: 75x6x3 with 4+ reps in reserve\, so 1RM is ne
 arer 100 - autoregulate to 2 REPS IN RESERVE and add 5 kg when the last 
 set still feels easy)\, LOADED UNILATERAL Bulgarian split squat 3 x 8/le
 g with dumbbells\, and TEMPO ECCENTRIC step-downs 3 x 8-10/leg with 3-4 
 s lowering. Then Nordics 3 x 5 and single-leg calf raises. Never to fail
 ure. 48-72 h before the long day. On a -15% descent hip drop is 23.7 mm 
 vs 7.6 mm uphill (very large effect)\, so descending is a frontal-plane 
 hip problem and not only a quad problem - loaded Bulgarians carry that d
 emand\, which is why standalone side planks and cable abduction came out
 . HYROX SLED TECHNIQUE at the end\, 8-10 x 12.5 m at 50-65% load (~100 k
 g)\, 60-90 s rest. TECHNIQUE ONLY\, never to fatigue. Forearms hooked on
  the posts\, 30-45 deg lean\, short choppy steps 20-30 cm at 3-4 per sec
 ond\, and never let the sled stop. Sled push is PURELY CONCENTRIC\, so i
 t costs your descent block nothing - which is why it is the one Hyrox st
 ation you can train now. At 56 kg you need 1.03x bodyweight of horizonta
 l force to break a stationary sled versus 0.81x to keep one rolling\, so
  learning not to stop is worth more to you than to anyone heavier. About
  8 minutes. LOWER-LEG CAPACITY\, about 4 min at the end: tibialis anteri
 or raises 3 x 15-20 (heels on a step\, toes lifting)\, heel walks 2 x 20
  m\, and eccentric dorsiflexion 3 x 10 slow against a band. The plan had
  NOTHING for the anterior lower leg and that is the tissue that failed o
 n the 7 Sep time trial - it is also what controls the foot down on every
  descending step\, which is 2\,003 m of Madeira. Progress the load week 
 to week. Keep the soleus and calf work as well\; this is added capacity\
 , not a substitution.\n\nWeek 11 of 17 - Build\nTime trial week. Vertica
 l drops for one week only\; six more weeks of it remain. All three stren
 gth sessions kept - only the VO2max session goes\, replaced by the trial
 .\n45 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w11-s4-pull@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Pull (upper)
DESCRIPTION:Pull (upper) - moved to Tuesday. Upper body only\, nothing th
 at loads the legs: the time trial is Wednesday and legs stay fresh until
  it is done. Pull (upper) - after the vertical session. HYROX SEEDING\, 
 all substitutions not additions: (1) WARM UP ON THE SKIERG OR ROWER\, 5-
 8 min\, technique only - hinge and drive the first third of the pull\, t
 hat is where 80% of ski power comes from. Replaces your normal warm-up\,
  costs nothing. (2) SWAP one row variation for a HEAVY FARMERS CARRY\, 4
  x 40-60 m. Same pulling pattern\, direct Hyrox transfer. (3) Finish wit
 h DEAD HANGS\, 3 x max. Baseline 20 Aug was 32/36/31 s\, so 90 s by Octo
 ber was never realistic: target 55-60 s by 1 Nov and 90 s by Hyrox in Ja
 nuary. Grip takes 4-6 weeks to change and it is what limits the farmers 
 carry. About 3 minutes total added to the session.\n\nWeek 11 of 17 - Bu
 ild\nTime trial week. Vertical drops for one week only\; six more weeks 
 of it remain. All three strength sessions kept - only the VO2max session
  goes\, replaced by the trial.\n47 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w11-s5-long@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260919
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260920
SUMMARY:▲ LONG DAY 2:30\, 600 m vert (16 km)
DESCRIPTION:LONG DAY 2:30\, 600 m vert - trimmed from 2:35/900 m. Your be
 st long-day vertical ever is 118 m\, so week 10's 500 m was already a fo
 ur-fold jump\; 600 m here keeps the ladder at 500 -> 600 -> 700 rather t
 han a 50% step onto ground you have never covered - Posbank if possible\
 , descents on hard surface DESCENT CUE: shorten the step\, 185-195 spm. 
 Understriding cut strength loss to -8.8% vs -15.5% at preferred step len
 gth - roughly halved. Do NOT coach foot strike: the more anterior the st
 rike\, the LARGER the quad torque loss. Let the terrain dictate it.\n\nW
 eek 11 of 17 - Build\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nTi
 me trial week. Vertical drops for one week only\; six more weeks of it r
 emain. All three strength sessions kept - only the VO2max session goes\,
  replaced by the trial.\n43 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w11-s6-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Easy run 30-40 MIN\, HR under 155. TIME TRIAL…
DESCRIPTION:Easy run 30-40 MIN\, HR under 155. TIME TRIAL WEEK - this is 
 a shakeout\, not a session. The VO2max block comes back in week 12. Add 
 4 x 20 s strides at the end\, relaxed\, full recovery.\n\nWeek 11 of 17 
 - Build\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nTime trial week
 . Vertical drops for one week only\; six more weeks of it remain. All th
 ree strength sessions kept - only the VO2max session goes\, replaced by 
 the trial.\n48 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
