DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260924
SUMMARY:Easy run 50 MIN (6.8 km)
DESCRIPTION:Easy run 50 MIN (talk test) + 6-8 x 20 s strides after (relax
 ed\, full recovery\, not a workout) PRESCRIBED IN MINUTES\, not kilometr
 es: at 7:20/km your 5 km was 36 min\, and the accepted easy-run band is 
 30-75 min. Kilometres make the dose shrink as you get faster\, which is 
 backwards. HR CEILING 155 - HARD RULE\, not a talk test. You already fix
 ed this: since 24 Aug your easy running is about 80% below 160 bpm\, up 
 from roughly 50% over June to mid-August. The number is here to hold the
  habit\, not to correct you. Novice guidance is about 85% genuinely easy
 . If holding 155 means walking the bridges\, walk them - pace is the out
 put here\, not the target.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Build\nKeep HR under 158. 
 Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~2\,000-2\,3
 00 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in mountain ultras heart rate FAL
 LS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. Pace off kne
 e-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the watch. PROGRESS METRIC: d
 o not judge fitness off pace-at-HR inside the VO2max reps - 3 min is too
  short for HR to settle and accumulated fatigue distorts it. Use a STAND
 ARDISED EASY RUN instead: same route\, same target HR\, track the pace m
 onth to month. That is the signal that replaces retesting until mid-Nove
 mber.\n39 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
