BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s4-vertical@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:▲ VERTICAL 75 min STEADY
DESCRIPTION:VERTICAL 75 min STEADY - stairwell\, your own building or a c
 ar park. WALK UP\, LIFT DOWN. This is a CLIMBING session and the descent
  is NOT the point: riding down keeps the eccentric cost at zero\, which 
 is deliberate\, because the descent stimulus is dosed separately\, in th
 e 5 min weighted preconditioning walks (weeks 12 and 15 - one bout prote
 cts for 4-8 weeks\, which is why they are spaced and not weekly). Target
  ~750 m\, about 17 x 15 floors\, at roughly 600 m/h including lift trans
 itions - already about twice Madeira's race climb rate of ~310 m/h\, so 
 it should feel steady and conversational\, not hard. TIME IS THE PRESCRI
 PTION and vertical is only the check: finishing near 600 m is fine\, do 
 not chase the number by rushing the climbs. NO INTERVALS - the hard sess
 ion is on Monday on flat ground\, because Hyrox is 8 x 1 km flat and sta
 ir fitness does not transfer to flat running economy. Dutch stair pitch 
 is 30-33 deg\, inside the optimal climbing range.\n\nWeek 12 of 17 - Bui
 ld\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~2\,000-2\,300 m. HR is now unreliabl
 e as a guide: in mountain ultras heart rate FALLS ~34 bpm across the rac
 e while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. Pace off knee-extensor RPE - how your
  quads feel - not the watch. PROGRESS METRIC: do not judge fitness off p
 ace-at-HR inside the VO2max reps - 3 min is too short for HR to settle a
 nd accumulated fatigue distorts it. Use a STANDARDISED EASY RUN instead:
  same route\, same target HR\, track the pace month to month. That is th
 e signal that replaces retesting until mid-November.\n38 days to Ultra X
  Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
