 put here\, not the target.\n\nWeek 13 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover
 \, do not add volume.\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nC
 utback before the two biggest weeks. Eat. At 56 kg with ~50 kg FFM you n
 eed at least 2\,250 kcal before exercise is counted - peak-week days run
  4\,800-5\,000 kcal. Under-fuelling an 11-week ramp is the most likely r
 oute to a stress fracture\, and your body mass must not trend down. PROG
 RESS METRIC: do not judge fitness off pace-at-HR inside the VO2max reps 
 - 3 min is too short for HR to settle and accumulated fatigue distorts i
 t. Use a STANDARDISED EASY RUN instead: same route\, same target HR\, tr
 ack the pace month to month. That is the signal that replaces retesting 
 until mid-November.\n32 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
