DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:◆ Legs ONLY\, no upper
DESCRIPTION:Legs ONLY\, no upper - maintenance. Volume down\, load held a
 t 80%+ 1RM. HYROX SLED TECHNIQUE at the end\, 8-10 x 12.5 m at 50-65% lo
 ad (~100 kg)\, 60-90 s rest. TECHNIQUE ONLY\, never to fatigue. Forearms
  hooked on the posts\, 30-45 deg lean\, short choppy steps 20-30 cm at 3
 -4 per second\, and never let the sled stop. Sled push is PURELY CONCENT
 RIC\, so it costs your descent block nothing - which is why it is the on
 e Hyrox station you can train now. At 56 kg you need 1.03x bodyweight of
  horizontal force to break a stationary sled versus 0.81x to keep one ro
 lling\, so learning not to stop is worth more to you than to anyone heav
 ier. About 8 minutes. LOWER-LEG CAPACITY\, about 4 min at the end: tibia
 lis anterior raises 3 x 15-20 (heels on a step\, toes lifting)\, heel wa
 lks 2 x 20 m\, and eccentric dorsiflexion 3 x 10 slow against a band. Th
 e plan had NOTHING for the anterior lower leg and that is the tissue tha
 t failed on the 7 Sep time trial - it is also what controls the foot dow
 n on every descending step\, which is 2\,003 m of Madeira. Progress the 
 load week to week. Keep the soleus and calf work as well\; this is added
  capacity\, not a substitution.\n\nWeek 13 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - re
 cover\, do not add volume.\nCutback before the two biggest weeks. Eat. A
 t 56 kg with ~50 kg FFM you need at least 2\,250 kcal before exercise is
  counted - peak-week days run 4\,800-5\,000 kcal. Under-fuelling an 11-w
 eek ramp is the most likely route to a stress fracture\, and your body m
 ass must not trend down. PROGRESS METRIC: do not judge fitness off pace-
 at-HR inside the VO2max reps - 3 min is too short for HR to settle and a
 ccumulated fatigue distorts it. Use a STANDARDISED EASY RUN instead: sam
 e route\, same target HR\, track the pace month to month. That is the si
 gnal that replaces retesting until mid-November.\n33 days to Ultra X Mad
 eira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w13-s4-vertical@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:▲ VERTICAL 45 min STEADY
DESCRIPTION:VERTICAL 45 min STEADY - stairwell\, your own building or a c
 ar park. WALK UP\, LIFT DOWN. This is a CLIMBING session and the descent
  is NOT the point: riding down keeps the eccentric cost at zero\, which 
 is deliberate\, because the descent stimulus is dosed separately\, in th
 e 5 min weighted preconditioning walks (weeks 12 and 15 - one bout prote
 cts for 4-8 weeks\, which is why they are spaced and not weekly). Target
  ~450 m\, about 10 x 15 floors\, at roughly 600 m/h including lift trans
 itions - already about twice Madeira's race climb rate of ~310 m/h\, so 
 it should feel steady and conversational\, not hard. TIME IS THE PRESCRI
 PTION and vertical is only the check: finishing near 360 m is fine\, do 
 not chase the number by rushing the climbs. NO INTERVALS - the hard sess
 ion is on Monday on flat ground\, because Hyrox is 8 x 1 km flat and sta
 ir fitness does not transfer to flat running economy. Dutch stair pitch 
 is 30-33 deg\, inside the optimal climbing range.\n\nWeek 13 of 17 - Bui
 ld\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volume.\nCutback before the two big
 gest weeks. Eat. At 56 kg with ~50 kg FFM you need at least 2\,250 kcal 
 before exercise is counted - peak-week days run 4\,800-5\,000 kcal. Unde
 r-fuelling an 11-week ramp is the most likely route to a stress fracture
 \, and your body mass must not trend down. PROGRESS METRIC: do not judge
  fitness off pace-at-HR inside the VO2max reps - 3 min is too short for 
 HR to settle and accumulated fatigue distorts it. Use a STANDARDISED EAS
 Y RUN instead: same route\, same target HR\, track the pace month to mon
 th. That is the signal that replaces retesting until mid-November.\n31 d
 ays to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w13-s5-pull@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Pull (upper)
DESCRIPTION:Pull (upper) - after the vertical session. HYROX SEEDING\, al
 l substitutions not additions: (1) WARM UP ON THE SKIERG OR ROWER\, 5-8 
 min\, technique only - hinge and drive the first third of the pull\, tha
 t is where 80% of ski power comes from. Replaces your normal warm-up\, c
 osts nothing. (2) SWAP one row variation for a HEAVY FARMERS CARRY\, 4 x
  40-60 m. Same pulling pattern\, direct Hyrox transfer. (3) Finish with 
 DEAD HANGS\, 3 x max. Baseline 20 Aug was 32/36/31 s\, so 90 s by Octobe
 r was never realistic: target 55-60 s by 1 Nov and 90 s by Hyrox in Janu
 ary. Grip takes 4-6 weeks to change and it is what limits the farmers ca
 rry. About 3 minutes total added to the session.\n\nWeek 13 of 17 - Buil
 d\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volume.\nCutback before the two bigg
 est weeks. Eat. At 56 kg with ~50 kg FFM you need at least 2\,250 kcal b
 efore exercise is counted - peak-week days run 4\,800-5\,000 kcal. Under
 -fuelling an 11-week ramp is the most likely route to a stress fracture\
 , and your body mass must not trend down. PROGRESS METRIC: do not judge 
 fitness off pace-at-HR inside the VO2max reps - 3 min is too short for H
 R to settle and accumulated fatigue distorts it. Use a STANDARDISED EASY
  RUN instead: same route\, same target HR\, track the pace month to mont
 h. That is the signal that replaces retesting until mid-November.\n31 da
 ys to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
