BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w13-s8-descent@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:▼ DESCENT LADDER (10 min)
DESCRIPTION:DESCENT LADDER - 10 min walking DOWN stairs with 5.6 kg in th
 e pack\, lift back up. About 220 m of descent. THIS IS THE SESSION THE P
 LAN USED TO BE MISSING: Madeira is 2\,003 m DOWN as well as up\, and dow
 nhill running causes far more muscle damage and neuromuscular fatigue th
 an level running at the same metabolic cost. One bout protects for weeks
  (repeated-bout effect)\, which is why this is dosed weekly and progress
 ively rather than repeated at 5 min. Stairs build tissue tolerance\; the
 y do NOT reproduce running descent mechanics\, which is what the Posbank
  long days are for.\n\nWeek 13 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do n
 ot add volume.\nCutback before the two biggest weeks. Eat. At 56 kg with
  ~50 kg FFM you need at least 2\,250 kcal before exercise is counted - p
 eak-week days run 4\,800-5\,000 kcal. Under-fuelling an 11-week ramp is 
 the most likely route to a stress fracture\, and your body mass must not
  trend down. PROGRESS METRIC: do not judge fitness off pace-at-HR inside
  the VO2max reps - 3 min is too short for HR to settle and accumulated f
 atigue distorts it. Use a STANDARDISED EASY RUN instead: same route\, sa
 me target HR\, track the pace month to month. That is the signal that re
 places retesting until mid-November.\n33 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w14-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:○ OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min - Sunday is now a REST day by de
 fault. Take the ride only if you feel good and Monday's run is easy. Wit
 h a quality session on Monday you need this rest more than you need the 
 ride.\n\nWeek 14 of 17 - Peak\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #2 - POSBANK AGAIN\, not 
 the Ardennes. Roughly EUR 30 of petrol against EUR 200\, and twenty reps
  of a 90-110 m climb is 1\,800 m of ascent AND hard-surface descent - cl
 ose to the whole race. Sustained descending on firm ground is the one th
 ing stairs cannot replicate\, and it is what decides your day. POLES: bo
 ught 18-20 Sep\, so you have had three weeks on them by now. Use them th
 e whole session. They cut RPE 14-18% and measurably reduce muscle damage
  over a climb-and-descent day - but an inexperienced pole user in a fiel
 d study actually got SLOWER\, so the practice is the point. KIT-CHECK HA
 BIT STARTS HERE: every food item must be labelled with its calorie count
 \, and all disposable packaging must carry your bib number. Tape a strip
  on your gel flask reading contents and total kcal (e.g. '4x Upfront Gel
  PRO - 640 kcal'). Do it from this session on\, not at registration.\n28
  days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w14-s1-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261007
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261008
SUMMARY:Easy run 55 MIN (7.5 km)
DESCRIPTION:Easy run 55 MIN (talk test) + 6-8 x 20 s strides after (relax
 ed\, full recovery\, not a workout) PRESCRIBED IN MINUTES\, not kilometr
 es: at 7:20/km your 5 km was 36 min\, and the accepted easy-run band is 
 30-75 min. Kilometres make the dose shrink as you get faster\, which is 
 backwards. HR CEILING 155 - HARD RULE\, not a talk test. You already fix
 ed this: since 24 Aug your easy running is about 80% below 160 bpm\, up 
 from roughly 50% over June to mid-August. The number is here to hold the
  habit\, not to correct you. Novice guidance is about 85% genuinely easy
 . If holding 155 means walking the bridges\, walk them - pace is the out
 put here\, not the target.\n\nWeek 14 of 17 - Peak\nKeep HR under 158. W
 alk the climbs. Talk test.\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #2 - POSBANK AGAIN\, not the
  Ardennes. Roughly EUR 30 of petrol against EUR 200\, and twenty reps of
  a 90-110 m climb is 1\,800 m of ascent AND hard-surface descent - close
  to the whole race. Sustained descending on firm ground is the one thing
  stairs cannot replicate\, and it is what decides your day. POLES: bough
 t 18-20 Sep\, so you have had three weeks on them by now. Use them the w
 hole session. They cut RPE 14-18% and measurably reduce muscle damage ov
 er a climb-and-descent day - but an inexperienced pole user in a field s
 tudy actually got SLOWER\, so the practice is the point. KIT-CHECK HABIT
  STARTS HERE: every food item must be labelled with its calorie count\, 
 and all disposable packaging must carry your bib number. Tape a strip on
  your gel flask reading contents and total kcal (e.g. '4x Upfront Gel PR
 O - 640 kcal'). Do it from this session on\, not at registration.\n25 da
 ys to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
