 nty reps of a 90-110 m climb is 1\,800 m of ascent AND hard-surface desc
 ent - close to the whole race. Sustained descending on firm ground is th
 e one thing stairs cannot replicate\, and it is what decides your day. P
 OLES: bought 18-20 Sep\, so you have had three weeks on them by now. Use
  them the whole session. They cut RPE 14-18% and measurably reduce muscl
 e damage over a climb-and-descent day - but an inexperienced pole user i
