DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261006
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261007
SUMMARY:▼ DESCENT LADDER (16 min)
DESCRIPTION:DESCENT LADDER - 16 min walking DOWN stairs with 5.6 kg in th
 e pack\, lift back up. About 352 m of descent. THIS IS THE SESSION THE P
 LAN USED TO BE MISSING: Madeira is 2\,003 m DOWN as well as up\, and dow
 nhill running causes far more muscle damage and neuromuscular fatigue th
 an level running at the same metabolic cost. One bout protects for weeks
  (repeated-bout effect)\, which is why this is dosed weekly and progress
 ively rather than repeated at 5 min. Stairs build tissue tolerance\; the
 y do NOT reproduce running descent mechanics\, which is what the Posbank
  long days are for.\n\nWeek 14 of 17 - Peak\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #2 - POSBAN
 K AGAIN\, not the Ardennes. Roughly EUR 30 of petrol against EUR 200\, a
 nd twenty reps of a 90-110 m climb is 1\,800 m of ascent AND hard-surfac
 e descent - close to the whole race. Sustained descending on firm ground
  is the one thing stairs cannot replicate\, and it is what decides your 
 day. POLES: bought 18-20 Sep\, so you have had three weeks on them by no
 w. Use them the whole session. They cut RPE 14-18% and measurably reduce
  muscle damage over a climb-and-descent day - but an inexperienced pole 
 user in a field study actually got SLOWER\, so the practice is the point
 . KIT-CHECK HABIT STARTS HERE: every food item must be labelled with its
  calorie count\, and all disposable packaging must carry your bib number
 . Tape a strip on your gel flask reading contents and total kcal (e.g. '
 4x Upfront Gel PRO - 640 kcal'). Do it from this session on\, not at reg
 istration.\n26 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w15-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
SUMMARY:○ OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min
DESCRIPTION:OPTIONAL easy spin 45-60 min - Sunday is now a REST day by de
 fault. Take the ride only if you feel good and Monday's run is easy. Wit
 h a quality session on Monday you need this rest more than you need the 
 ride.\n\nWeek 15 of 17 - Peak\nPEAK WEEKEND - Sat 17 Oct\, 15 days out. 
 This is the overload the taper is built on\; the evidence favours peakin
 g 14-15 days out\, not five weeks. 3:45-4:00 and 1\,600-1\,800 m: roughl
 y 60-70% of race duration but 80-90% of race vertical. Vertical specific
 ity is the lever\, not duration.\n21 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w15-s1-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261014
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261015
SUMMARY:Easy run 50 MIN (6.8 km)
DESCRIPTION:Easy run 50 MIN (talk test) + 6-8 x 20 s strides after (relax
 ed\, full recovery\, not a workout) PRESCRIBED IN MINUTES\, not kilometr
 es: at 7:20/km your 5 km was 36 min\, and the accepted easy-run band is 
 30-75 min. Kilometres make the dose shrink as you get faster\, which is 
 backwards. HR CEILING 155 - HARD RULE\, not a talk test. You already fix
 ed this: since 24 Aug your easy running is about 80% below 160 bpm\, up 
 from roughly 50% over June to mid-August. The number is here to hold the
  habit\, not to correct you. Novice guidance is about 85% genuinely easy
 . If holding 155 means walking the bridges\, walk them - pace is the out
 put here\, not the target.\n\nWeek 15 of 17 - Peak\nKeep HR under 158. W
 alk the climbs. Talk test.\nPEAK WEEKEND - Sat 17 Oct\, 15 days out. Thi
 s is the overload the taper is built on\; the evidence favours peaking 1
 4-15 days out\, not five weeks. 3:45-4:00 and 1\,600-1\,800 m: roughly 6
 0-70% of race duration but 80-90% of race vertical. Vertical specificity
  is the lever\, not duration.\n18 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
