END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w15-s3-legs@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261013
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261014
SUMMARY:◆ Legs ONLY\, no upper
DESCRIPTION:Legs ONLY\, no upper - heavy eccentric. Three quad lifts doin
 g three different jobs: HEAVY BILATERAL trap-bar deadlift 4 x 4-6 at 85 
 kg (18 Aug: 75x6x3 with 4+ reps in reserve\, so 1RM is nearer 100 - auto
 regulate to 2 REPS IN RESERVE and add 5 kg when the last set still feels
  easy)\, LOADED UNILATERAL Bulgarian split squat 3 x 8/leg with dumbbell
 s\, and TEMPO ECCENTRIC step-downs 3 x 8-10/leg with 3-4 s lowering. The
 n Nordics 3 x 5 and single-leg calf raises. Never to failure. 48-72 h be
 fore the long day. On a -15% descent hip drop is 23.7 mm vs 7.6 mm uphil
 l (very large effect)\, so descending is a frontal-plane hip problem and
  not only a quad problem - loaded Bulgarians carry that demand\, which i
 s why standalone side planks and cable abduction came out. HYROX SLED TE
 CHNIQUE at the end\, 8-10 x 12.5 m at 50-65% load (~100 kg)\, 60-90 s re
 st. TECHNIQUE ONLY\, never to fatigue. Forearms hooked on the posts\, 30
 -45 deg lean\, short choppy steps 20-30 cm at 3-4 per second\, and never
  let the sled stop. Sled push is PURELY CONCENTRIC\, so it costs your de
 scent block nothing - which is why it is the one Hyrox station you can t
 rain now. At 56 kg you need 1.03x bodyweight of horizontal force to brea
 k a stationary sled versus 0.81x to keep one rolling\, so learning not t
 o stop is worth more to you than to anyone heavier. About 8 minutes. LOW
 ER-LEG CAPACITY\, about 4 min at the end: tibialis anterior raises 3 x 1
 5-20 (heels on a step\, toes lifting)\, heel walks 2 x 20 m\, and eccent
 ric dorsiflexion 3 x 10 slow against a band. The plan had NOTHING for th
 e anterior lower leg and that is the tissue that failed on the 7 Sep tim
 e trial - it is also what controls the foot down on every descending ste
 p\, which is 2\,003 m of Madeira. Progress the load week to week. Keep t
 he soleus and calf work as well\; this is added capacity\, not a substit
 ution.\n\nWeek 15 of 17 - Peak\nPEAK WEEKEND - Sat 17 Oct\, 15 days out.
  This is the overload the taper is built on\; the evidence favours peaki
 ng 14-15 days out\, not five weeks. 3:45-4:00 and 1\,600-1\,800 m: rough
 ly 60-70% of race duration but 80-90% of race vertical. Vertical specifi
 city is the lever\, not duration.\n19 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w15-s4-vertical@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:▲ VERTICAL 80 min STEADY
DESCRIPTION:VERTICAL 80 min STEADY - stairwell\, your own building or a c
 ar park. WALK UP\, LIFT DOWN. This is a CLIMBING session and the descent
  is NOT the point: riding down keeps the eccentric cost at zero\, which 
 is deliberate\, because the descent stimulus is dosed separately\, in th
 e 5 min weighted preconditioning walks (weeks 12 and 15 - one bout prote
 cts for 4-8 weeks\, which is why they are spaced and not weekly). Target
  ~800 m\, about 18 x 15 floors\, at roughly 600 m/h including lift trans
 itions - already about twice Madeira's race climb rate of ~310 m/h\, so 
 it should feel steady and conversational\, not hard. TIME IS THE PRESCRI
 PTION and vertical is only the check: finishing near 640 m is fine\, do 
 not chase the number by rushing the climbs. NO INTERVALS - the hard sess
 ion is on Monday on flat ground\, because Hyrox is 8 x 1 km flat and sta
 ir fitness does not transfer to flat running economy. Dutch stair pitch 
 is 30-33 deg\, inside the optimal climbing range.\n\nWeek 15 of 17 - Pea
 k\nPEAK WEEKEND - Sat 17 Oct\, 15 days out. This is the overload the tap
 er is built on\; the evidence favours peaking 14-15 days out\, not five 
 weeks. 3:45-4:00 and 1\,600-1\,800 m: roughly 60-70% of race duration bu
 t 80-90% of race vertical. Vertical specificity is the lever\, not durat
 ion.\n17 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w15-s5-pull@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Pull (upper)
DESCRIPTION:Pull (upper) - after the vertical session. HYROX SEEDING\, al
 l substitutions not additions: (1) WARM UP ON THE SKIERG OR ROWER\, 5-8 
 min\, technique only - hinge and drive the first third of the pull\, tha
 t is where 80% of ski power comes from. Replaces your normal warm-up\, c
 osts nothing. (2) SWAP one row variation for a HEAVY FARMERS CARRY\, 4 x
  40-60 m. Same pulling pattern\, direct Hyrox transfer. (3) Finish with 
 DEAD HANGS\, 3 x max. Baseline 20 Aug was 32/36/31 s\, so 90 s by Octobe
 r was never realistic: target 55-60 s by 1 Nov and 90 s by Hyrox in Janu
 ary. Grip takes 4-6 weeks to change and it is what limits the farmers ca
 rry. About 3 minutes total added to the session.\n\nWeek 15 of 17 - Peak
 \nPEAK WEEKEND - Sat 17 Oct\, 15 days out. This is the overload the tape
 r is built on\; the evidence favours peaking 14-15 days out\, not five w
 eeks. 3:45-4:00 and 1\,600-1\,800 m: roughly 60-70% of race duration but
  80-90% of race vertical. Vertical specificity is the lever\, not durati
 on.\n17 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w15-s6-long@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:▲ PEAK LONG DAY 3:45-4:00\, 1000 m vert. Race kit\,…
DESCRIPTION:PEAK LONG DAY 3:45-4:00\, 1000 m vert. Race kit\, poles\, rac
 e fuelling\, race shoes. Alternate 20-25 min climbing with 15-20 min fla
 t to rehearse the sawtooth. DESCENT CUE: shorten the step\, 185-195 spm.
  Understriding cut strength loss to -8.8% vs -15.5% at preferred step le
 ngth - roughly halved. Do NOT coach foot strike: the more anterior the s
 trike\, the LARGER the quad torque loss. Let the terrain dictate it. POS
 BANK - MANDATORY. Stairs and the StairMaster give you climbing and zero 
 descent\, and vertical stepping does not transfer to running mechanics. 
 This is one of only three sessions in the block where you actually run d
 ownhill on terrain. Do not substitute it.\n\nWeek 15 of 17 - Peak\nKeep 
 HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nPEAK WEEKEND - Sat 17 Oct\, 1
 5 days out. This is the overload the taper is built on\; the evidence fa
 vours peaking 14-15 days out\, not five weeks. 3:45-4:00 and 1\,600-1\,8
 00 m: roughly 60-70% of race duration but 80-90% of race vertical. Verti
 cal specificity is the lever\, not duration.\n15 days to Ultra X Madeira
  25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
