SUMMARY:▼ DESCENT LADDER (20 min)
DESCRIPTION:DESCENT LADDER - 20 min walking DOWN stairs with 5.6 kg in th
 e pack\, lift back up. About 440 m of descent. THIS IS THE SESSION THE P
 LAN USED TO BE MISSING: Madeira is 2\,003 m DOWN as well as up\, and dow
 nhill running causes far more muscle damage and neuromuscular fatigue th
 an level running at the same metabolic cost. One bout protects for weeks
  (repeated-bout effect)\, which is why this is dosed weekly and progress
 ively rather than repeated at 5 min. Stairs build tissue tolerance\; the
 y do NOT reproduce running descent mechanics\, which is what the Posbank
  long days are for. FINAL HARD DESCENT BOUT - this is the last one that 
 matters. Two weeks out is the timing the evidence gives: long enough to 
 recover\, close enough that the repeated-bout protection is still live o
 n race day.\n\nWeek 15 of 17 - Peak\nPEAK WEEKEND - Sat 17 Oct\, 15 days
