BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w16-s6-descent@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260908T124212Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261020
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261021
SUMMARY:▼ DESCENT LADDER (6 min)
DESCRIPTION:DESCENT LADDER - 6 min walking DOWN stairs with 5.6 kg in the
  pack\, lift back up. About 132 m of descent. THIS IS THE SESSION THE PL
 AN USED TO BE MISSING: Madeira is 2\,003 m DOWN as well as up\, and down
 hill running causes far more muscle damage and neuromuscular fatigue tha
 n level running at the same metabolic cost. One bout protects for weeks 
 (repeated-bout effect)\, which is why this is dosed weekly and progressi
 vely rather than repeated at 5 min. Stairs build tissue tolerance\; they
  do NOT reproduce running descent mechanics\, which is what the Posbank 
 long days are for. PRIMER ONLY\, not a session - keep it short and unloa
 ded-feeling. The protective work is already done.\n\nWeek 16 of 17 - Tap
 er\nTaper starts. Volume down 45-55%\, intensity and frequency UNCHANGED
  - that combination is worth 2-3%\, about 7-11 minutes on a 6-hour race.
  NOTHING ECCENTRIC AFTER 21 OCTOBER. Last heavy lower-body work is done.
 \n12 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
